<title>USA: Isis shares rise after milestone payment.</title>
<headline>Isis shares rise after milestone payment.</headline>
<dateline>CARLSBAD, Calif. 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isis Pharmaceuticals said it received a $10 million milestone payment from Boehringer Ingelheim after a clinical trial of one of its antisense prohibitors, ISIS 2302.</p>
<p>Under terms of the payment, Boehringer Ingelheim will invest $10 million in Isis at $24.47 a share.</p>
<p>Isis said after completing the first Phase IIa clinical trial of ISIS 2302 in Crohn's disease, an inflammatory bowel disease, it and Boehringer Ingelheim are planning a large Phase IIb trial in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Isis shares jumped 3-1/8 to 19-7/8 in early trading.</p>
</text>
